<!--
  A STIPULATION, NOT A FILING. See assets/fixtures/README.md.

  A composed figure filed as a `fusionSum` derivation: an output of its fusion, which the receiver
  computes.

    pair     line-a + line-b, less one order both lines count     demand DERIVED  [29, 34, 41]
    site     pair + line-c                                         demand stated   [34, 40, 49]
    single   line-d alone                                          draw DERIVED, over a draw
                                                                   nobody metered
    plant    single + line-e                                       draw stated, over a part
                                                                   whose draw cannot be computed;
                                                                   nameplate DERIVED  [6 + 8 = 14]

  `site`'s demand can only be checked by computing `pair`'s, which is a part of it and states no
  demand of its own: [10 + 20 - 1, 12 + 24 - 2, 14 + 30 - 3] = [29, 34, 41], then
  [29 + 5, 34 + 6, 41 + 8] = [34, 40, 49]. `single`'s draw cannot be computed at all, because the
  one part it would come from files its draw `unmeasured`, and that has to be said rather than
  read as a gap in `single`. So `plant`, which is built on `single`, owes no draw sum: the sum
  would read a part with no figure, and it is lifted with that part's reason. Its demand sum is
  owed as usual, and its nameplate is itself a derivation, so it is computed from its parts'
  ratings rather than checked against them.

  Every figure is in orders per day, every nameplate is a point, and every layer is a clearance.
-->
